      <title>Rare desert plant thrives at Nevada solar site, offering lessons for the Mountain West</title>
      <link>https://www.kunr.org/local-stories/2026-01-28/rare-desert-plant-thrives-nevada-solar-site</link>
      <description>As large solar projects become more common across the Mountain West, questions remain about their environmental footprint, especially in fragile desert ecosystems. New research from Nevada suggests that with careful planning, renewable energy development and rare native plants may be able to coexist.</description>
